    "2026-10-02": "Vendor pages and model-list endpoints re-read for the census extension (data/census_ext_models.json): gemini-2.0-flash family retired 2026-06-01, gpt-3.5-turbo-0125 and gpt-5-pro-2025-10-06 on the OpenAI retirement table, claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929 deprecated 2026-09-30, Gemini 2.5 and 3 previews retired; all added by scripts/census_refresh.py",
    "2026-10-11": "Vendor pages re-read before submission (snapshots data/vendor_pages/openai_deprecations_2026-10-11.md, anthropic_model_deprecations_2026-10-11.md, google_gemini_deprecations_2026-10-11.md). All 75 dates match the pages except gemini-1.0-pro and text-bison, moved from 2025-04-09 to 2025-04-21 (Vertex model-versions table). No announcement after 2026-10-02 enters the vocabulary: OpenAI's newest is 2026-10-01 (gpt-5.1, gpt-5.3-codex, gpt-5.4-nano, shutdown 2027-04-01), Anthropic's 2026-09-30, Google's 2026-10-08 deprecations carry no date. Text identifiers with published dates that the vocabulary does not track: gpt-3.5-turbo-1106, gpt-3.5-turbo-instruct, babbage-002, davinci-002 (retired 2026-09-28; on the page since 2025-09-26), the specialized OpenAI variants retired in 2026 (codex, chat-latest, deep-research, search and computer-use previews) and the 2026-10-01 announcement.",
    "2026-10-11 refresh": "scripts/census_refresh2.py: gpt-3.5-turbo-instruct and gpt-3.5-turbo-1106 (retired 2026-09-28, announced 2025-09-26) harvested on 2026-10-11 (babbage-002 and davinci-002, harvested in the same run, are not tracked: the phrase search cannot separate them from text-davinci-002 and text-babbage-001); gpt-5.1, gpt-5.1-2025-11-13, gpt-5.4-nano, gpt-5.4-nano-2026-03-17 (retirement 2027-04-01, announced 2026-10-01) folded in from the extension harvest; the gpt-3.5-turbo alias now resolves to gpt-3.5-turbo-1106 between 2023-12-11 and 2024-02-15. Not tracked, by scope: the specialized variants the OpenAI page lists under its three-month notice policy (codex, chat-latest, deep-research, search and computer-use previews) and the audio, image, video, embedding and moderation models.",
    "2026-10-12 refresh": "scripts/census_refresh3.py: the three vendor pages as read on 2026-10-11 were re-read against the completeness rule recorded in 'completeness_rule'; the remaining language-model identifiers with a published retirement date were harvested on 2026-10-12 and folded in (text-ada-001, text-babbage-001, code-davinci-002, code-davinci-001, code-cushman-001, code-cushman-002, gpt-4-turbo-preview, gpt-5, gpt-5-mini, gpt-5-nano, claude-1.0, claude-1.1, claude-1.2, claude-1.3, claude-instant-1.0, claude-instant-1.1, claude-instant-1, claude-instant, claude-2.0, claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022, claude-3-haiku-20240307, claude-3-5-haiku-20241022, claude-3-7-sonnet-20250219, claude-opus-4, claude-sonnet-4, claude-opus-4-1, gemini-pro-vision, gemini-1.0-pro-vision, chat-bison, code-gecko, gemini-2.0-flash-exp, gemini-2.0-pro-exp, gemini-2.0-flash-thinking-exp, gemini-2.5-pro-exp-03-25, gemini-2.0-flash-lite-preview, gemini-2.5-flash-lite-preview-06-17). Excluded by the rule: ambiguous phrases (ada, babbage, curie, davinci, babbage-002, davinci-002, gemini-pro), non-text modalities, the specialized tool products under OpenAI's three-month notice policy and Gemini computer-use, fine-tuning names, and the Gemini 2.5 / 3.6 / 3.7 models whose Vertex dates the Gemini API page contradicts."
  },
  "completeness_rule": "Included: every identifier of a text-generating model (chat, completion, code completion) on the OpenAI, Anthropic and Google Gemini/Vertex pages that carries a published retirement date, as a dated snapshot or as a dateless alias that a date window resolves to a retired snapshot. Excluded, by stated rule: (a) phrases that OpenAlex full-text search cannot separate from another identifier (ada, babbage, curie, davinci, babbage-002, davinci-002, gemini-pro); (b) non-text modalities (audio, speech, image, video, embeddings, moderation, realtime); (c) the specialized tool products the OpenAI page files under its three-month notice policy (codex agents, deep-research, search and computer-use previews, the moving -chat-latest aliases, gpt-5.4-cyber) and Gemini computer-use, because they are agent endpoints rather than model snapshots a paper pins and several have no published release date; (d) fine-tuning names (ft-*); (e) identifiers whose retirement is announced on one Google surface but denied on the other (gemini-2.5-pro/-flash/-flash-lite, gemini-3.6-flash, gemini-3.7-flash: Vertex dates, Gemini API 'until further notice'), kept in the extension census as still served."
